<title>JAPAN: Forex moves not result of verbal intervention - MOF.</title>
<headline>Forex moves not result of verbal intervention - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recent movements in foreign exchange rates were not the result of verbal intervention, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told a parliamentary committee meeting on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Recent movements of exchange rates are not due to verbal intervention,&quot; Mitsuzuka said in response to a committee member's view that they were.</p>
<p>The finance minister also reiterated that it was important for the economy hat exchange rates stabilise. -- Tokyo Policy Desk +81-3-5473-3710</p>
</text>
